	Unlikely.  Large customers with large checkbooks lined up for large 
	orders.  Contractural promises, etc.  Besides, I think Itanium2 systems
	will be out and about before EV7 at year-end.

> 
> Will IA64 V2.0 have "world's fastest chip" status if it comes out this summer
> with the speed estimates, or will it still be eclipsed by Power and the 2.4ghz
> 8086 ?
> 

	Depends on the metric or what is measured.  I'll bet we will
	see some sort of RSA benchmark.

> Is there any chance that it would be faster than EV7 ?

	Depends on the metric.  Expect large floating point numbers.  Not
	nearly the integer number.  Large tpmC , but Oracle and SQL help there.
	I would speculate it is faster in one,  RSA.  Close in floating
	point (close being within 10% but that is a guess).  I'm not certain
	of a large CPU count McKinley running Oracle (which OS)?  But surely
	we will see a large SQL number with many cobbled together 8 processor
	boxes, like so:

