Hi,

I've done a few of these upgrades over the past couple of years, whilst
working as a Consultant for a Compaq reseller in the UK.

There is no simple upgrade path from Compaq, as you are throwing out the HSZ
controllers and putting in new ones. You can save the config to a file on
laptop, but in my experience, writing down the config is quicker and more
reliable.

You need to save the raid set info so you can reconstruct it when you put
the new controllers in. You will need to supply new unit numbers, since the
numbering scheme is no longer SCSI unit number based.

If you are booting from the RA8000, then you will need to set the persistent
reservation table so that the HSG based units are visible at boot time.

4.0x doesn't support multi-pathing very well, so be careful how you wire up
the SAN.

Edit the fstab file to re-mount your file systems.

Document your config well before the upgrade and it's not a particularly
scary procedure!

Cheers

--
Regards,

David Burnett

