news:3CE56D02.5ADF8F10@videotron.ca...

...

> If non-VMS clusters do not have distributed lock managers,

Well, at least two non-VMS clusters (Tru64 and IBM p-Series) do have (clones
of) the VMS DLM.

 how do they deal
> with one node depositing a message in my mailbox while another node is
> accessing and deleting messages from the same mailbox ?

Some single node serves the section of storage your mailbox is on, and
coordinates locks to clients (as NFS lock servers do).  I suppose in some
sense this qualifies as 'distributed locking' (since multiple clients can
hold at least instantaneous locks on the same data) but it certainly doesn't
match the VMS facilities (and falls more under the class of centralized
algorithms than distributed ones).

- bill





