prevent
> reads and/or writes to the volume while files are moved ?

If you can have both disk sets present at once, why bother with that? Just
create a new domain on the new set and do a backup/restore. That way you can
star fresh a the new disk and set parameters (if any). On Digital UNIX 4.0D
I would do:

Server:/# mkfdmn -p 7200 -x 512 -l 1024 /dev/... new_domain
Server:/# mkfset new_domain new
Server:/# mount -t advfs new_domain#new /mnt
Server:/# vdump -0 -f - /oracle7 | (cd /mnt ; vrestore -x -f -)

Nix.




