You'll want to make sure that the disk can be seen at the SRM prompt.  If 
the console can't see it, then the kernel is not likely to see it, either.

You might want to post some more information, like:

        - what kind of alpha?
        - SCSI adapter type that the disk will attach to
        - make/model of disk (size, too)
        - type of enclosure that the disk is in


If the SCSI adapter is already known to the kernel, then it'll find 
whatever disks are attached to the adapter -- no kernel rebuild is 
necessary.  

But first, the console has to see the disk.

        Stu


