On 22 May 2002 06:17:22 -0700, gary_matthews@bigfoot.com
(Welshboy) wrote:

>Hi 
>Are there any free tools I can use to check perfromance on my TRU64
>system? Our DBAs are blaming the storageworks box we've got connected
>for performance issues, and I'm looking for something that can
>prove/disprove. (DB is Oracle). Being a complete newbie to TRU64 any
>point in the right direction would be much appreciated.

iostat will tell you if you have I/O problems -- if you have high
system wait % or long wait times/% on the controllers (>30) or
drives, you have I/O problems. 
You and the DBAs have to understand both drive and Oracle I/O
configs and requirements for performance, and any special
considerations for Tru64. 
That means you have to read the Oracle docs about I/O config and
DBAs have to read the drive docs about config. 
In simplified terms, for actively updated table spaces, raid 5 is
bad, raid 0+1 is good, NVRAM is good; large memory is good, lots
of processors are good.
Setting Oracle parameters to encourage full table scans is bad,
encourage index use is good; parallel query is only good if you
really have to do lots of full tabel scans. 
Using default cost based optimizer without analysis of all tables
and daily analysis of updated tables is bad. 
Using rule based optimizer without understanding rules for
writing queries is bad. 

