As I said, the term cluster has become horribly overloaded. This isn't
good. I wish it hadn't, but we have to live in a world where lots of
people use the term for lots of different things.

This is what I have largely been trying to say, Your definition of cluster
is not the only one. It might be a good one, but it's not the only one.

I guess if pushed I'd define a cluster as

"A group of systems cooperating together"


