Your right, for HP-UX 8 some joker put the DUX stuff onto the 800 series
I never did find anyone who had even thought of using it. It was way to slow
to do any IO intensive stuff on. On the other hand almost all workstation sites
used it, many even when all systems had local disks. It was easy to manage.



>
>         I am sure part of the impetus for creating a "true" cluster (all
>         disk resources shared) was the fact that storage was not cheap
>         20 years ago.
