>new to Tru64, so any advice would be greatly appreciated.

You don't say exactly what you mean by "12MB memory space"....
Data size? Malloc'able space? Program text size?

Anyway, the place to start is:

8:20am > limit
cputime         unlimited
filesize        unlimited
datasize        1310720 kbytes
stacksize       8192 kbytes
coredumpsize    unlimited
memoryuse       484264 kbytes
descriptors     4096 

The datasize here is set to 1280MB, 10 times what you indicate.

The other thing to look at is:

8:20am > sysconfig -q proc
proc:
max_proc_per_user = 256
max_threads_per_user = 1024
per_proc_stack_size = 8388608
max_per_proc_stack_size = 33554432
per_proc_data_size = 1342177280
max_per_proc_data_size = 1073741824
max_per_proc_address_space = 4294967296
per_proc_address_space = 4294967296
 ...


These can be tuned pretty easily. Look at "man sys_attrs_proc" to
find out how and what they do.

