pui ming Wong (<ac0j0j$15r6$1@net44p.hkbu.edu.hk>):

> 
> What's the procedure to add a 3rd party (seagate to be exact)
> external scsi disk to the alpha
> Must i be able to see its existence
> in the SRM console first before doing the steps like
> Makedev (and newfs)
> under the OS level
> Now I've just added an external h/d  and restarted the machine but
> doing the command
> show device under >>>  prompt
> just doesn't show it
> Does it matter, or i just simply proceed to do the MAKEDEV ?

Case the drive is connected to an external controller, you may need 
to set it up, as explained in the controller documentation, there's 
no need to reboot, most controller allow adding a new hd on the fly.

Case you made the hd known to the controller and you are running 
4.0, you need to run:

# scu scan edt
Try now
# scu show edt

It should be visible. If you have the right /dev, you can procees 
writting a label to the hd. Case you are using version >4.0, you 
need to take a look at 'man hwmgr'.

Good luck

