try

find / -mount -mtime -9 -print

which will find all files on the root modified in the last 9 days (or 
make that when the disk started filling up) and you might find something 
that's been growing out of control.

find / -mount -size +999 -print

to find files of 999 blocks (or choose another value) and see if there 
are any suspicious large files around.

If you can't find the cause you might want to boot single user and run 
fsck on the root file system.

finally when you've sorted it out it's probably a good idea to move the 
/tmp onto another partition if you can do so.



