calls
> > 'shared storage', since each host has direct physical access to the
storage
> > (analogous to the shared memory in an SMP) and shares it essentially
> > concurrently.  'Shared-nothing' usually refers to a system where each
> > storage unit (and each unit of everything else, like memory) is private
to
> > some host and accessible only through that host (even though that host
may
> > export it for shared use as VMS exports MSCP devices - which is
sometimes
> > called pseudo-shared storage).
> >
