In article <abhu8a$j0o$1@news1.kornet.net> "Atom" <aiguru@linux.co.kr> writes:
>How I get cpu total number and online cpu number by table() system call on
>tru64..

Table() isn't what you want; getsysinfo() is. From the getsysinfo man page:

  GSI_CPUS_IN_BOX
      Returns the actual number of CPUs present in the current machine in the
      form of an int.

      buffer
          int

      nbytes
          Specifies the size of the user buffer.

My code snippet:

#include <sys/sysinfo.h>

        int ncpus;
        getsysinfo(GSI_CPUS_IN_BOX, (char *)&ncpus, sizeof(ncpus), 0L, 0L, 0L);
        printf ("There are %d CPUs in this box\n", ncpus);

