> quick review of the ssh website gives me the impression that it is only
> "sort of" supported for DU (I have systems running V4.0D and F). The
> website mentions availability of source code only for this system.
> Does anyone have more detailed knowledge of the availability of ssh for DU?

We have a web kit of ssh available that has been enhanced to work better
with Tru64 UNIX.  I think this is your best bet for getting ssh to work
seamlessly with Tru64 UNIX, but this version of ssh will only work with 
V5.1a, so it would mean you would have to upgrade:
http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/unix/ssh/
In V5.1b ssh will be integrated into Tru64 UNIX.

I don't know about the compatibility of ssh with V4.0* beyond what you
see on their web site.  If you're stuck with V4.0* you might want to look
at openssh as well to see if it would work better for you.

> Also, does it implement more or less the same features as Enhanced
> Security or is it more far reaching? Thanks, in advance, for any
> information.

ssh and Enhanced Security are totally different things.  The Security
Guide is the place to go for information on Enhanced Security.  The
enhancements in Enhanced Security are mostly in the areas of enhanced
Identification and Authentication (e.g. more and better secured
user account information).  Ssh mostly secures remote connections
(i.e. replaces ftp, rsh, rcp, etc).  So, in many cases, it wouldn't
be a bad idea to have both Enhanced Security and ssh.


