Well, you've obviously turned on Enhanced Security, or you
wouldn't be getting those messages.  My first suggestion is
that you read up on Enhanced Security starting with the Security
manual and the prpasswd, edauth, default, and authcap man pages.

You may have just turned off logging of unsuccessful logins in
the default file.  Logging of unsuccessful logins is turned off if
the "d_skip_fail_login_log" entry exists in the default database
and the entry is not followed by an @.  

You could try making other changes to the database (i.e. change
your password) to see if you have a general problem accessing
the database.


