>1 gb for Quorum

Quorum disk can be very very small. 1 GB is a massive waste. The cluster 
subsystems only use 1MB of the disk !!!! 
But this disk can't have anything else on it !!!!

If your using a HS* controller to raid your disks then I'd just creation a
partition with the controller (which is presented to the OS as a separate disk)
which is say 10MB in size for the quorum disk.

For further details on disks required for clustering see :-

