A multi-volume domain created on Tru64 UNIX v4.* _SHOULD_ work on 
version v5.*.  Have you tried running verify against the domain?

On v5.* there is a new utility called /sbin/advfs/fixfdmn which should 
correct any metadata errors in the domain and hopefully allow it to be 
successfully mounted on a v5.1 system.

However, if you still want to convert the domain to the v5.* on-disk 
format, then you will need to 

        backup
        create new domain
        restore from backup

If you have sufficient spare disk space, then you could also

        create new domain on spare disks
        create fileset
        mount new domain
        vdump -0 -f - /mount_point | vrestore -xf - -D /new_domain_mnt

                                        Bob Harris


