reason to buy their flavor of *nix.  The world is going to wind up with
Windows, Linux and proprietary operation systems.  With OpenVMS, NSK and
Tru64/HP-UX,  HP rivals IBM as king of the proprietary OS.

The real question (which is still unanswered) is: does HP view it's
proprietary OS's as a competitive advantage that should be promoted in order
to advance it's position in all three arenas or as a cash cow that should be
milked until it can convert everyone to a Linux or Windows environment?

I hope they answer that question soon.





